  "discovered_via": "manufacturer product page link list, fetched 2026-10-09",
  "summary": "Single-channel isolated gate-driver board (board Rev 7.0) for discrete Wolfspeed SiC MOSFETs: TI UCC23514 opto-compatible isolated driver, separate turn-on/turn-off path using a steering diode, provisional Miller clamp pin, and a discrete 2 W isolated bias supply built from the TI UCC25800 open-loop LLC transformer driver, a Wurth 750319177 transformer, voltage-doubler rectifier and Zener/resistor split into approximately +15 V / -3.3 V.",
  "license": {
    "redistribution": "not-verified",
    "terms_source": "document footers and Important Notes (PRD-08391 pp.18-20)",
    "notes": "Wolfspeed documents carry '(c) Wolfspeed, Inc. All rights reserved'; no redistribution licence was found in the documents or design-file archives inspected. Treated as not redistributable; only original analysis and metadata are committed."
  },
  "evidence_limitations": [
    "PRD-08391 Table 1 values were extracted from PDF text in which footnote markers are fused with numbers (e.g. '8003 Vpk' = 800 Vpk with note 3, '22 W' = 2 W with note 2); values were reconciled against the footnotes and Figure 5 load range (0-2 W).",
    "The steering-diode direction for D3 was determined from the schematic symbol (cathode on the driver VOUT side) and the series connection with R7 confirmed from the ODB++ netlist; the netlist itself carries no diode polarity.",
    "The board has no DESAT/overcurrent protection; it is an evaluation board for discrete devices, so protection knowledge is not derived from it.",
    "Measured performance is limited to the bias-supply regulation plot (Figure 5); switching waveforms are not published in the user guide."
  ],
  "analysis": "analysis.md",
  "ratings": {
    "supply_voltage": "11-12.5 V (12 V typ.)",
    "output_levels": "+15.4 V / -3.3 V typical",
    "peak_output_current": "+4.5 A / -5.31 A (driver IC, depends on gate resistors)",
    "bias_power": "2 W at 25 degC (table footnote marker fused into value in text extraction)",
    "isolation": "800 Vpk basic per transformer rating (IEC 61558-2-16, OVC II, PD2)",
    "operating_temperature": "0-50 degC",
    "board_revision": "7.0"
  },
  "source_discrepancies": [
    "User guide states rails are regulated 'within 5%' by a 15 V and a 3.9 V Zener, while Table 1 lists VOL = -3.3 V typical (lower than the 3.9 V Zener) - the negative rail is therefore not simply the Zener voltage under all loads.",
    "User guide revision history labels the document Rev 4 (October 2024) while the cover only shows PRD-08391; the design files are board Rev 7.0 dated June 2024."
  ]
}
